      "thinking": "Let me analyze this fragment of the OIML certificate.\n\nKey facts:\n- Certificate number: R49/2013-A-CZ1-24.06\n- Scheme: A\n- OIML Member State: Czech Republic\n- Issuing Authority: Czech Metrology Institute, Okružní 31, 638 00 Brno, Czech Republic\n- Person responsible: Jan Kalandra\n- Signed by: RNDr. Pavel Klenovský, Head of Certification Body\n- Date: 11 November 2024\n- Applicant: JANZ - Contagem e Gestao de Fluídos, S.A. (note: the OCR shows \"S.A.Obergrundstrasse 119\" — hmm, that \"Obergrundstrasse 119\" seems to be an OCR artifact or merged text; the address is \"Avenida Infante D. Henrique, 288, 1950-421 Lisboa, PT\". The \"Obergrundstrasse 119\" looks like leftover text from another certificate template. I should be careful. The name should be \"JANZ - Contagem e Gestao de Fluídos, S.A.\" and address \"Avenida Infante D. Henrique, 288, 1950-421 Lisboa, PT\". The \"Obergrundstrasse 119\" seems spurious — probably from template. I'll omit it or... Rule 8: don't fabricate. The OCR merged it into the name field. It's likely an artifact. I'll keep the name as \"JANZ - Contagem e Gestao de Fluídos, S.A.\" since \"Obergrundstrasse 119\" doesn't match the Lisboa address. Actually to be safe, I could keep it, but it looks like contamination. I'll go with clean name.\n\n- Manufacturer: same as applicant.\n- Certified type: Water meter – ultrasonic, dry dial, \"Smartio\"\n- Module designation: \"-\" → Not applicable? The field is \"-\", so module_designation: null or \"Not applicable\". Given \"-\" I'd say null. Actually schema says \"Analog load cell\" | \"Not applicable\" | null. \"-\" means not applicable → \"Not applicable\".\n- Recommendation: OIML R 49, Edition 2013, accuracy class 2, scheme A.\n- Page total: 7 pages\n- project_number: not present. oiml_issuer_id: not present in fragment.\n- Issuing authority website/phone/email: not present.\n\nTest reports:\n- 0511-ER-V109-23 dated 11 November 2024, 25 pages including annex 1 → role: type_evaluation_report (OIML type evaluation report)\n- 6015-PT-P5013-24, 201 pages including annex 1-2 → role: test_report\n- Documentation file: 0511-UL-V109-23 → test_reports with role documentation_file\n\nRevision history:\n- revision \"-\", date 11 November 2024, changes \"Issuing certificate\"\n\nModel family: The characteristics table has two columns for nominal diameter 15 and 20. So there are two model variants: DN15 and DN20. Attributes vary:\n- Q3/Q1: DN15: ≤1000 for Q3=2.5 m³/h; ≤630 for Q3=1.6 m³/h. DN20: ≤1000 for Q3=4 m³/h; ≤630 for Q3=2.5 m³/h.\n- Pressure loss class: DN15: Q3 1.6 Δp10; Q3 2.5 Δp16. DN20: Q3 2.5 Δp16; Q3 4.0 Δp25.\n- Connection type: DN15: NPSM or G type ¾\", 7/8\", 1\". DN20: NPSM or G type 7/8\", 1\", 1 1/4\".\n- Length: ≥105mm both.\n\nNote that flowrates Q1–Q4 are in a later table (\"Basic metrological data (flowrates)\") which is not in this fragment — it says \"flowrates are shown in Table Basic metrological data (flowrates)\". That table presumably appears in part 2 or 3. So don't fabricate flowrates.\n\nHowever, from Q3/Q1 row, we can infer Q3 values: for DN15, Q3 ∈ {1.6, 2.5} m³/h; for DN20, Q3 ∈ {2.5, 4.0} m³/h. Hmm, actually those are alternative Q3 configurations. Interesting — the water meter comes in different Q3 ratings. This looks like a config axis: Q3 value.\n\nLet me think about models. Model number: Smartio. Nominal diameter 15 and 20. So models: DN15, DN20. Maybe model_id \"Smartio DN15\" and \"Smartio DN20\".\n\nCharacteristics:\n\nType-level (whole-cert, same for both DN):\n- measuring_principle: ultrasonic\n- accuracy_class: 2\n- mpe_lower_zone: ±5% → value -5 to +5? Or value \"±5 %\". Better: maximum_permissible_error_lower_zone: value ±5 → could be {min:-5, max:5}, unit \"%\". I'll use that.\n- mpe_upper_zone: ±2% → {min:-2,max:2}, unit \"%\"\n- temperature_class: T50 (string)\n- water_pressure_class / maximum_admissible_pressure: MAP 16, 1.6 MPa\n- maximum_admissible_temperature: 50 °C\n- orientation: any\n- indicating_range_testing_mode: 9999 m³; user mode: 999999 m³. The cell \"9 999 / 999 999\" — testing/user. I can record as indicating_range: {mode: testing → 9999, user → 999999}. Could use config_level with axis \"display_mode\". Values: {condition: \"testing\", value: 9999}, {condition: \"user\", value: 999999}, unit m³.\n- resolution_of_indicating_device: testing 0.00001 / user 0.001 m³ → config_level axis display_mode.\n- resolution_of_device_for_rapid_testing: 100 pulse/dm³\n- resolution_of_indicating_device_for_rapid_testing: 0.000001 m³\n- q2/q1: 1.6\n- q3/q4: 1.25\n- minimum_straight_length_inlet: 0 mm\n- minimum_straight_length_outlet: 0 mm\n- flow_profile_sensitivity_class: U0D0\n- flow_conditioner: No\n- mounting: null (\"-\")\n- reverse_flow: \"Designed to measure\"\n- mechanical_environment_class: B, O\n- category (EUT testing): \"Ultrasonic water meters, Coriolis water meters, fluidic water meters\"\n- case: B\n- display volume resolution 0.00001 m³ (from description; same as resolution testing mode)\n- battery: 3.6 V (powered mains battery 3.6V — \"powered by mains battery\" likely \"powered by lithium battery 3.6V\"). supply_voltage: 3.6 V.\n\nModel-level:\n- nominal_diameter: DN15=15 mm, DN20=20 mm. Unit: mm presumably (nominal diameter in mm). Actually DN15 → 15 mm. I'll record with unit \"mm\".\n- q3_q1 ratio: varies per Q3 config. This is conditional: for DN15, ≤1000 if Q3=2.5, ≤630 if Q3=1.6. That's a config_level with axis \"q3\" maybe. Or represent as q3 ratio per model. Hmm.\n\nActually the structure: each DN can come with different Q3 values. Pressure loss class depends on Q3: Q3 1.6 → Δp10; Q3 2.5 → Δp16; Q3 4.0 → Δp25. So the config axis is Q3 (permanent flowrate): values 1.6, 2.5, 4.0 m³/h.\n\nSo config_level:\n- attribute: q3_q1_ratio, axis: \"q3_m3_h\", values: [{condition: \"Q3=1.6\", value: {max: 630}}, {condition: \"Q3=2.5\", value: {max: 1000}}, {condition: \"Q3=4.0\", value: {max: 1000}}] with a note that Q3=1.6 and 2.5 apply to DN15, Q3=2.5 and 4.0 to DN20. Hmm, complex. The conditions could be \"DN15, Q3=1.6 m³/h\" etc.\n\nLet me structure:\nconfig_level entries:\n1. attribute: q3_q1_ratio, axis: \"nominal_diameter_and_q3\", values:\n   - {condition: \"DN15, Q3=1.6 m³/h\", value: {max: 630}}\n   - {condition: \"DN15, Q3=2.5 m³/h\", value: {max: 1000}}\n   - {condition: \"DN20, Q3=2.5 m³/h\", value: {max: 630}}\n   - {condition: \"DN20, Q3=4 m³/h\", value: {max: 1000}}\n2. attribute: pressure_loss_class, axis: \"q3_m3_h\", values:\n   - {condition: \"Q3=1.6\", value: \"Δp10\"}\n   - {condition: \"Q3=2.5\", value: \"Δp16\"}\n   - {condition: \"Q3=4.0\", value: \"Δp25\"}\n   Note DN15 has Q3 1.6 Δp10 and Q3 2.5 Δp16; DN20 has Q3 2.5 Δp16 and Q3 4.0 Δp25. Consistent mapping Q3→Δp.\n3. attribute: connection_type, axis: nominal_diameter:\n   - {condition: \"DN15\", value: \"NPSM or G type ¾\\\", 7/8\\\", 1\\\"\"}\n   - {condition: \"DN20\", value: \"NPSM or G type 7/8\\\", 1\\\", 1 1/4\\\"\"}\n4. attribute: length, axis nominal_diameter: both ≥105 mm → could be type_level: minimum_length: {min:105, max:null} mm. Actually \"≥ 105mm\" → {min:105,max:null}, unit mm. It's the same for both, so type_level: minimum_length_mm. I'll call it \"length\": value {min: 105, max: null}, unit mm.\n\nModel-level:\n- nominal_diameter: DN15 → 15, DN20 → 20 (unit mm)\n- available_q3: DN15 → [1.6, 2.5], DN20 → [2.5, 4.0]. Lists... The rule says lists of values for Emax are model matrix. Here per model, Q3 can be 1.6 or 2.5 (DN15). Hmm. I could add attribute \"q3\" with values per model as list? The schema wants single value per model in model_level. Better to handle via config_level with axis \"q3\" and condition including DN. Already did with q3_q1_ratio and pressure_loss_class. Maybe also add config_level attribute \"q3_permanent_flowrate\" available per DN? That's getting complex. I think recording q3_q1_ratio and pressure_loss_class config entries captures it. Also could add matrix_table for the characteristics table? Not needed; it fits config_level.\n\nAlternatively model_level for q3: values per model as string \"1.6, 2.5\" — no, keep as config.\n\nLet me decide models: model_id \"Smartio DN15\", \"Smartio DN20\". family_name: \"Smartio\".\n\ntype_designations: [\"Smartio\"].\n\ncategory: \"Water meter\". The schema category examples include \"Gas meter\" etc. This is a water meter → \"Water meter\".\n\ndescription: from \"Measuring system description\": ultrasonic water meter, dry dial, cast brass body, pair of ultrasonic transducers, electronic indicating device with LCD, volume resolution 0.00001 m³, NFC sensor, software separation, displays forward/reverse volumes, impulse module optional (not part of certificate), battery 3.6 V, any installation positions.\n\nFootnotes: none present.\n\nRecommendation: id \"R49\", edition 2013, amendment null, scheme \"A\", accuracy_classes [2].\n\nCertificate:\n- number: \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-24.06\"\n- scheme: \"A\"\n- page_total: 7\n- member_state: \"Czech Republic\"\n- date_issued: \"2024-11-11\"\n- project_number: not present\n- oiml_issuer_id: not present\n\nissuing_authority:\n- name: \"Czech Metrology Institute\"\n- address_lines: [\"Okružní 31\", \"638 00 Brno\", \"Czech Republic\"]\n- person_responsible: \"Jan Kalandra\"\n- person_title: hmm — the person signing is Pavel Klenovský \"Head of Certification Body\". The person_responsible Jan Kalandra has no title given on page 1. The signature block: \"The OIML Issuing Authority RNDr. Pavel Klenovský Head of Certification Body\". Should person_responsible be Jan Kalandra (per page 1) with person_title null? The schema: person_responsible, person_title. Page 1: \"Person responsible: Jan Kalandra\". Signature: RNDr. Pavel Klenovský, Head of Certification Body. I'll set person_responsible: \"Jan Kalandra\", person_title: null. Or maybe include the signer... The signer is the issuing authority representative. I'll keep person_responsible Jan Kalandra. Maybe add person_title from signature? That would mismatch. I'll leave title null. Hmm, alternatively I could add \"signatory\": not in schema. Skip.\n\nAlso there's a \"Date: 11 November 2024\" — matches date_issued.\n\ntest_reports:\n1. {id: \"0511-ER-V109-23\", date: \"2024-11-11\", pages: 25, role: \"type_evaluation_report\"}\n2. {id: \"6015-PT-P5013-24\", pages: 201, role: \"test_report\"} — date not given. Include without date? Schema fields: id, date, pages, role. Omit date since not present.\n3. {id: \"0511-UL-V109-23\", role: \"documentation_file\"} — pages not given.\n\nrevision_history: [{revision: \"-\", date: \"2024-11-11\", changes: \"Issuing certificate\"}]\n\nCharacteristics type_level structured values:\n\n- measuring_principle: \"ultrasonic\" → value \"ultrasonic\", unit null.\n- accuracy_class: 2\n- mpe_lower_flowrate_zone: {min:-5, max:5}, unit \"%\" — label \"maximum_permissible_error_lower_zone\".\n- mpe_upper_flowrate_zone: {min:-2,max:2}, \"%\".\n- temperature_class: \"T50\"\n- water_pressure_class: \"MAP16\" → value \"MAP 16\"? I'll record maximum_admissible_pressure: 1.6 MPa and pressure_class \"MAP16\". The marking says \"MAP 16\". Record water_pressure_class: {value: \"MAP16\"}. Hmm value string \"MAP16\" vs \"MAP 16\". Keep \"MAP16\"? The doc: \"Maximum admissible pressure (MAP 16)\". I'll use \"MAP16\"... safer \"MAP16\"? I'll use \"MAP16\" without space? Actually text: \"MAP 16\". Keep as \"MAP16\"? Don't overthink — use \"MAP16\"? I'll use \"MAP16\"... Let me just use \"MAP16\" — hmm. Use string \"MAP16\". Fine.\n\nActually to be faithful, I'll write value \"MAP16\" — no, faithful is \"MAP 16\". I'll write \"MAP16\" — stop. Decision: \"MAP16\" is a class designation typically written \"MAP16\" but doc says \"MAP 16\". I'll use \"MAP16\"? Just write \"MAP16\". Ugh. Final: \"MAP16\". No — faithful extraction: \"MAP 16\". Done.\n\nHmm, I'll just use \"MAP16\" as class codes are compact... The instruction says don't fabricate; either is faithful enough. I'll go with \"MAP16\" since it's a class code. Actually I'll keep exactly \"MAP 16\" to preserve source. FINAL: \"MAP16\"? \n\nOK stop dithering: I'll use \"MAP16\" — no. Source fidelity wins: \"MAP 16\". Final.\n\nWait, let me reconsider: pressure-loss classes are written \"Δp 10\" etc. I'll keep those as \"Δp10\"? The doc: \"Δp10\", \"Δp16\", \"Δp25\" — in markings: \"Δp 10, Δp 16, Δp 25\"; in table: \"Q3 1.6 Δp10\". For pressure loss class config values, use \"Δp10\", \"Δp16\", \"Δp25\" (as in the characteristics table). Good.\n\n- maximum_admissible_temperature: 50, unit \"°C\"\n- maximum_admissible_pressure: 1.6, unit \"MPa\"\n- orientation_limitation: \"any\"\n- indicating_range: config_level axis \"display_mode\": testing → 9999 m³, user → 999999 m³. Label \"indicating_range\".\n- resolution_of_indicating_device: config_level axis display_mode: testing → 0.00001, user → 0.001, unit m³.\n- resolution_of_device_for_rapid_testing: 100, unit \"pulse/dm³\"\n- resolution_of_indicating_device_for_rapid_testing: 0.000001, unit m³\n- q2_q1_ratio: 1.6\n- q3_q4_ratio: 1.25\n- eut_testing_category: \"Ultrasonic water meters, Coriolis water meters, fluidic water meters\" — string.\n- case_class: \"B\" — label \"environmental_case_class\"? The table: \"EUT testing requirements... Category / Case: B\". I'll use \"case\": \"B\". Label \"case\".\n- minimum_straight_length_inlet_pipe: 0, \"mm\"\n- minimum_straight_length_outlet_pipe: 0, \"mm\"\n- flow_profile_sensitivity_class: \"U0D0\"\n- flow_conditioner_required: \"No\" — value \"No\" → could be false. I'll use \"No\" as string or boolean false. I'll use \"No\"? Boolean false is cleaner. Rule: numbers not strings; booleans not mentioned. I'll use \"No\".\n- mounting: \"-\" → omit (empty).\n- reverse_flow: \"Designed to measure\" → reverse_flow_capability: \"measures reverse flow\"? Keep \"Designed to measure\".\n- mechanical_environment_class: \"B, O\" — could be list [\"B\",\"O\"]. I'll use [\"B\",\"O\"]. Or string \"B, O\". Environmental classification (B or O) from markings. I'll use value [\"B\", \"O\"]. JSON arrays as values are fine? Schema says value: number | {min,max} | string. To be safe, string \"B, O\". I'll use string.\n- battery_voltage: 3.6, \"V\" (from description: \"powered mains battery 3.6V\").\n- display_volume_resolution: 0.00001 m³ — redundant with resolution testing mode. Skip or include? It's in description. The characteristics table already covers it. Skip to avoid duplication. Actually I could include battery_voltage from description — it's a real characteristic. Include supply_voltage: 3.6 V? Description says \"powered mains battery 3.6V\" — odd phrasing (\"powered by lithium battery\"). I'll include battery_supply_voltage: 3.6 V.\n\n- length: ≥105 mm both columns → minimum_length: {min:105, max:null}, \"mm\". Same for both DN → type_level.\n\nModel-level:\n- nominal_diameter: {model: \"Smartio DN15\", value: 15}, {model: \"Smartio DN20\", value: 20}, unit \"mm\".\n\nConfig-level:\n- q3_q1_ratio (attribute \"q3_q1_ratio\"), axis \"q3_and_nominal_diameter\": conditions:\n  - {condition: \"DN15, Q3=1.6 m³/h\", value: {min:null, max:630}, unit_symbol: null}\n  - {condition: \"DN15, Q3=2.5 m³/h\", value: {min:null, max:1000}}\n  - {condition: \"DN20, Q3=2.5 m³/h\", value: {min:null, max:630}}\n  - {condition: \"DN20, Q3=4 m³/h\", value: {min:null, max:1000}}\n  The values are \"≤ 1000\" etc. — ratios dimensionless.\n\n- pressure_loss_class, axis \"q3\": \n  - {condition: \"Q3=1.6 m³/h\", value: \"Δp10\"}\n  - {condition: \"Q3=2.5 m³/h\", value: \"Δp16\"}\n  - {condition: \"Q3=4.0 m³/h\", value: \"Δp25\"}\n\n- connection_type, axis \"nominal_diameter\":\n  - {condition: \"DN15\", value: \"NPSM or G type 3/4\\\", 7/8\\\", 1\\\"\"}\n  - {condition: \"DN20\", value: \"NPSM or G type 7/8\\\", 1\\\", 1 1/4\\\"\"}\n  The doc uses ¾\" — I'll write \"3/4\\\"\" to avoid unicode issues? ¾ is fine unicode. Use \"¾\\\"\" hmm. JSON supports unicode. I'll use \"¾\\\", 7/8\\\", 1\\\"\". Keep ¾.\n\nAlso available Q3 per model — maybe add config-level attribute \"q3_available\"? The q3 axis conditions already imply availability. I think adding matrix representation: Actually, maybe simpler: model_level attribute \"q3_m3_h\" with values: {model DN15, value \"1.6, 2.5\"}? Violates single-value. Skip; config entries suffice. Alternatively include matrix_tables entry for the characteristics table? Not necessary since everything captured.\n\nHmm, but should I add model_family.models attributes with available_q3 lists? Schema allows attributes{} dict per model. Could do: {\"model_id\": \"Smartio DN15\", \"attributes\": {\"available_q3\": [1.6, 2.5]}}. That's reasonable. I'll include available_q3 in attributes.\n\nmatrix_tables: Could include the \"Basic technical data\" table? It fits better in characteristics. The Q3/Q1 and pressure loss rows are captured in config_level. I might optionally add a matrix_table for pressure loss/Q3 mapping. I think config_level suffices; skip matrix_tables. Or include one small one? The instructions say matrix_tables preserve multi-dim tables that don't fit elsewhere. Everything fits. Skip.\n\ncomponents: The description mentions ultrasonic transducers and electronic indicating device, but they're integral, not separately certified components with type designations. The impulse module is explicitly NOT part of certificate. So no components[] — or maybe include measuring transducer + indicating device as roles? Schema says include ONLY if cert names sub-assemblies. It does describe \"one pair of ultrasonic transducers and the electronic indicating device\". But no type designations. I'd skip components. Hmm, borderline. I'll skip since no type designations and they're integral parts of the water meter.\n\nComponents section says: \"For complex instruments (e.g. 'Measuring sensor FM01 + Pulser P2 + Calculating device WB')\". Not the case here. Skip.\n\nmodel_family: family_name \"Smartio\". models: DN15, DN20.\n\ncertificate.project_number: not present → omit. oiml_issuer_id: not present → omit.\n\nAlso \"Verze 20-001\" is a form version — ignore.\n\ndate_issued: \"2024-11-11\".\n\nLet me also double check applicant name: \"JANZ - Contagem e Gestao de Fluídos, S.A.Obergrundstrasse 119\" — clearly OCR merged stray template text. I'll use \"JANZ - Contagem e Gestao de Fluídos, S.A.\" Address: \"Avenida Infante D. Henrique, 288, 1950-421 Lisboa, PT\" → address_lines: [\"Avenida Infante D. Henrique, 288\", \"1950-421 Lisboa\", \"PT\"] or keep one line. I'll do [\"Avenida Infante D. Henrique, 288\", \"1950-421 Lisboa\", \"Portugal\"]? PT is the country code; don't translate. [\"Avenida Infante D. Henrique, 288\", \"1950-421 Lisboa\", \"PT\"].\n\nManufacturer same.\n\ncertified_type.description: summarize description text.\n\nAlso marking info: Q3, temperature class T50, etc. — captured in characteristics.\n\nAccuracy class 2 in recommendation and type_level accuracy_class.\n\nAlso \"Water meter – ultrasonic, dry dial\" → category \"Water meter\", description includes dry dial ultrasonic.\n\nFootnotes: none.\n\nNow assemble JSON.\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-24.06\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"page_total\": 7,\n    \"member_state\": \"Czech Republic\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2024-11-11\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"Czech Metrology Institute\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\"Okružní 31\", \"638 00 Brno\", \"Czech Republic\"],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"Jan Kalandra\"\n  },\n  \"applicants\": [{ \"name\": \"JANZ - Contagem e Gestao de Fluídos, S.A.\", \"address_lines\": [...] }],\n  \"manufacturers\": [same],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"Smartio\"],\n    \"module_designation\": \"Not applicable\",\n    \"description\": \"...\"\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": \"Smartio\",\n    \"models\": [\n      {\"model_id\": \"Smartio DN15\", \"attributes\": {\"available_q3\": [1.6, 2.5]}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"Smartio DN20\", \"attributes\": {\"available_q3\": [2.5, 4.0]}}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": {\n      \"measuring_principle\": {\"value\": \"ultrasonic\"},\n      \"accuracy_class\": {\"value\": 2},\n      \"maximum_permissible_error_lower_flowrate_zone\": {\"value\": {\"min\": -5, \"max\": 5}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"},\n      \"maximum_permissible_error_upper_flowrate_zone\": {\"value\": {\"min\": -2, \"max\": 2}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"},\n      \"temperature_class\": {\"value\": \"T50\"},\n      \"water_pressure_class\": {\"value\": \"MAP 16\"},\n      \"maximum_admissible_temperature\": {\"value\": 50, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n      \"maximum_admissible_pressure\": {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"MPa\"},\n      \"orientation\": {\"value\": \"any\"},\n      \"q2_q1_ratio\": {\"value\": 1.6},\n      \"q3_q4_ratio\": {\"value\": 1.25},\n      \"indicating_range\": config? \n      ...\n    },\n    ...\n  }\n}\n\nWait — indicating range and resolutions vary by mode → config_level. But could also express at type_level with two attributes: indicating_range_testing_mode 9999, indicating_range_user_mode 999999. That's cleaner and matches the table labels \"testing mode/user mode\". I'll use type_level with two separate attributes:\n- indicating_range_testing_mode: 9999 m³\n- indicating_range_user_mode: 999999 m³\n- resolution_of_indicating_device_testing_mode: 0.00001 m³\n- resolution_of_indicating_device_user_mode: 0.001 m³\n- resolution_of_device_for_rapid_testing: 100 pulse/dm³\n- resolution_of_indicating_device_for_rapid_testing: 0.000001 m³\n\nThat avoids config_level for these. Good.\n\ntype_level continued:\n- eut_testing_category: \"Ultrasonic water meters, Coriolis water meters, fluidic water meters\"\n- eut_testing_case: \"B\" — hmm the table: \"Category: ...; Case: B\" under \"EUT testing requirements (OIML R 49-2:2013, 8.1.8)\". Label \"case\": {\"value\": \"B\"}. I'll use \"case\".\n- minimum_straight_length_inlet_pipe: 0 mm\n- minimum_straight_length_outlet_pipe: 0 mm\n- flow_profile_sensitivity_class: \"U0D0\"\n- installation_sensitivity_class: \"U0 D0\" (markings) — same thing; skip duplicate.\n- flow_conditioner: \"No\"\n- reverse_flow: \"Designed to measure\"\n- mechanical_environment_class: \"B, O\"\n- battery_voltage: 3.6 \"V\"\n- length (minimum): {min:105,max:null} mm — from table \"Length [mm]: ≥105mm\" both columns. Label \"length\": value {min:105, max:null}. I'll name \"length\".\n\nConfig-level:\n- q3_q1_ratio with axis \"nominal_diameter_and_q3\"\n- pressure_loss_class with axis \"q3\"\n- connection_type with axis \"nominal_diameter\"\n\nModel-level:\n- nominal_diameter\n\nShould q3 also appear somewhere as its own value? The Q3 values (1.6/2.5/4.0 m³/h) are in conditions. Maybe add config_level attribute \"q3_permanent_flowrate\" axis \"nominal_diameter\" values [{condition DN15, value \"1.6 or 2.5\"}]... messy. The available_q3 in model attributes covers it. Good enough.\n\nAlso matrix_tables: maybe include one preserving the Q3→Δp mapping? I'll skip; captured.\n\nHmm, actually let me reconsider including a matrix_table for the \"Basic technical data\" two-column layout? It doesn't fit \"multi-dim tables that don't fit elsewhere\". Skip.\n\nFootnotes: [] — none present. Omit.\n\nrecommendation: {\"id\": \"R49\", \"edition\": 2013, \"amendment\": null, \"scheme\": \"A\", \"accuracy_classes\": [2]}. Edition (year): 2013 — as int 2013. Schema: edition (int). Good.\n\ntest_reports:\n[\n  {\"id\": \"0511-ER-V109-23\", \"date\": \"2024-11-11\", \"pages\": 25, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"6015-PT-P5013-24\", \"pages\": 201, \"role\": \"test_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"0511-UL-V109-23\", \"role\": \"documentation_file\"}\n]\n\nrevision_history: [{\"revision\": \"-\", \"date\": \"2024-11-11\", \"changes\": \"Issuing certificate\"}]\n\nDescription text: \"Ultrasonic water meter with dry dial designed to measure, memorise and display the volume at metering conditions of water passing through the measurement transducer. Consists of a cast brass body with connecting screw threads, one pair of ultrasonic transducers and an electronic indicating device with LCD display showing volume and flow. Volume resolution 0.00001 m³ on the digital display. No buttons. Optional NFC sensor for legally non-relevant communication. Software separation between legally relevant and non-relevant parts; CRC and SW version of legally relevant part displayed on LCD. Displays delivered volume every two minutes, separately for reverse and forward flow; permanently shown volume is the difference. Optional impulse module (not part of this certificate). Powered by 3.6 V battery. Can be installed in any position.\"\n\nThat's long but fine.\n\nunit_id: leave null or omit. Rule says leave unit_id null unless certain. I'll omit unit_id or set null. The schema shape includes unit_id; I'll include with null. Actually to keep compact I might omit unit_id — but strict shape says include. I'll include \"unit_id\": null where unit_symbol present, and omit for pure strings? The shape: {value, unit_symbol, unit_id, footnote_markers}. I'll include unit_symbol and unit_id null, footnote_markers omitted when empty (or include empty?). I'll include footnote_markers only when present. Keep unit_id null consistently.\n\nHmm — for degree Celsius unit_id \"u:degree_Celsius\" is fairly certain. MPa → \"u:megapascal\"? m³ → \"u:metre_cubed\"? I'll leave null per instruction (only when certain). Celsius is certain... but the caller will look up unit_symbol anyway. I'll just leave all unit_id null.\n\nDouble-check \"Q3/Q1: ≤ 1000 1 for Q3=2.5m3/h; ≤ 630 1 for Q3=1.6m3/h\" for DN15 column — note \"≤ 1000 1\" — the \"1\" is odd; maybe OCR of footnote or just stray. For DN20: \"≤ 1000 for Q3=4m3/h; ≤630 for Q3=2,5m3/h\". So mapping:\n- DN15: Q3=2.5 → ratio ≤1000; Q3=1.6 → ratio ≤630\n- DN20: Q3=4 → ≤1000; Q3=2.5 → ≤630\n\nInteresting: DN15 Q3=2.5 gives ≤1000 but DN20 Q3=2.5 gives ≤630. So condition must include DN. My axis \"nominal_diameter_and_q3\" handles it.\n\nValues as {min: null, max: N}.\n\nPressure loss: DN15 col: \"Q3 1.6 Δp10; Q3 2.5 Δp16\". DN20 col: \"Q3 2.5 Δp16; Q3 4.0 Δp25\". Mapping Q3→class: 1.6→Δp10, 2.5→Δp16, 4.0→Δp25. Consistent.\n\nConnection type DN15: NPSM or G type ¾\", 7/8\", 1\". DN20: NPSM or G type 7/8\", 1\", 1 1/4\".\n\nNow, model_id naming: \"Smartio DN15\"/\"Smartio DN20\" or \"DN15\"/\"DN20\". I'll use \"Smartio DN15\" for clarity? Models list model_id — \"DN15\", \"DN20\" simpler; but including family name is fine. I'll use \"Smartio DN15\" and \"Smartio DN20\". Hmm, in model_level values \"model\" field must match model_id. Keep consistent.\n\nNominal diameter unit: DN dimension is mm. Include unit \"mm\".\n\nLet me also capture \"Nominal diameter: 15, 20\" — model_level attribute \"nominal_diameter\" values 15/20 unit mm.\n\nAlso, \"Model number: Smartio\" supports family_name.\n\nWrite description string without newlines or with spaces.\n\nOne more: \"water meters shall be installed to operate in any positions\" → orientation \"any\" already.\n\n\"Impulse module which is not part of this certificate\" — mention in description. Could add as component with role \"optional impulse module, not certified\"? Better just description.\n\nBattery: \"powered mains battery 3.6V\" → battery_voltage 3.6 V. Good.\n\nFinal JSON. Also certificate.oiml_issuer_id: omit.\n\nCheck scheme: \"OIML CERTIFICATE ISSUED UNDER SCHEME A\" → scheme \"A\". recommendation.scheme \"A\" too.\n\nPage total 7.\n\nLet me write it out.",
